screen.LIGHTING=Lighting & Time of Day
screen.LIGHTING.comment=Name color = performance cost: \u00a7agreen\u00a7r = free, \u00a7eyellow\u00a7r = small cost, \u00a7cred\u00a7r = heavy
option.NIGHT_BRIGHTNESS=\u00a7aNight Brightness
option.NIGHT_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Brightness of the night sky, fog and moonlight on the world. 0 = pitch black night, only torches give light
option.DAY_GLOOM=\u00a7aDay Gloom
option.DAY_GLOOM.comment=Overcast daylight: dims the daytime sky and fog, deepens shadows in shaded places and mutes grass and leaf colors. 0 = normal bright day
option.CAVE_LIGHT=\u00a7aCave Daylight
option.CAVE_LIGHT.comment=How much daylight reaches cave mouths, overhangs and spots under trees. 0 = they go almost black. Deep caves stay dark at any value
option.TWILIGHT_STRENGTH=\u00a7aTwilight Tint
option.TWILIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Warm orange sunrise/sunset and blue dusk tint on the sky, fog and lighting. 0 = no tint
option.TWILIGHT_LENGTH=\u00a7aTwilight Length
option.TWILIGHT_LENGTH.comment=How long sunrise and sunset last. Lower = short and sharp, higher = longer and smoother transition between day and night

screen.SKY=Sky & Clouds
screen.SKY.comment=Name color = performance cost: \u00a7agreen\u00a7r = free, \u00a7eyellow\u00a7r = small cost, \u00a7cred\u00a7r = heavy
option.CLOUDS=\u00a7aClouds
option.CLOUDS.comment=Still, dark gray overcast covering the whole sky, like on a long rainy day. Off = plain sky gradient
option.CLOUD_DARKNESS=\u00a7aCloud Darkness
option.CLOUD_DARKNESS.comment=How dark the overcast sky and the fog are. Lower = lighter gray, higher = heavier and darker
option.CLOUD_VARIATION=\u00a7aCloud Variation
option.CLOUD_VARIATION.comment=Large soft lighter and darker patches in the overcast. 0 = perfectly even gray
option.CLOUD_HORIZON=\u00a7aClear Horizon Band
option.CLOUD_HORIZON.comment=Height in degrees above the horizon where the sky stays plain fog color without patches. Hides distant mountains at the render distance edge
option.SKY_COOL=\u00a7aSky Blue Tint
option.SKY_COOL.comment=Cold blue tint of the overcast sky and fog. 0 = neutral gray, 1 = noticeably blue

screen.LIGHTS=Dynamic Light
screen.LIGHTS.comment=Name color = performance cost: \u00a7agreen\u00a7r = free, \u00a7eyellow\u00a7r = small cost, \u00a7cred\u00a7r = heavy
option.TORCH_FLICKER=\u00a7aFire Flicker
option.TORCH_FLICKER.comment=Light from torches, fires and lava gently flickers. Torches and lanterns held in hands flicker too. Lamps may flicker slightly as well, the shader cannot tell them apart
option.FLICKER_STRENGTH=\u00a7aFlicker Strength
option.FLICKER_STRENGTH.comment=How much the brightness wavers. Higher = stronger, more noticeable flicker
option.FLICKER_SPEED=\u00a7aFlicker Speed
option.FLICKER_SPEED.comment=How fast the light wavers. Lower = calm slow breathing, higher = nervous fast flicker
option.HELD_LIGHT=\u00a7eHeld Item Light
option.HELD_LIGHT.comment=Torches, lanterns, glowstone and other glowing items light up the area around them: in your hands, in other mobs' hands, dropped on the ground and in item frames. Small FPS cost: every pixel checks the nearby light sources
option.HELD_LIGHT_STRENGTH=\u00a7aHeld Light Strength
option.HELD_LIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of the light from glowing items
option.HELD_LIGHT_RADIUS=\u00a7aHeld Light Radius
option.HELD_LIGHT_RADIUS.comment=How far the light reaches compared to the item's light level. 1 = as far as a placed block of the same item
option.PORTAL_LIGHT=\u00a7ePortal Light
option.PORTAL_LIGHT.comment=The nearest nether portal casts real purple light onto blocks around it. Small FPS cost: lit pixels read the portal position from a buffer
option.PORTAL_LIGHT_STRENGTH=\u00a7aPortal Light Strength
option.PORTAL_LIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of the purple light cast by the portal
option.PORTAL_LIGHT_RADIUS=\u00a7aPortal Light Radius
option.PORTAL_LIGHT_RADIUS.comment=How far the portal light reaches, in blocks
option.PORTAL_FRAME_TINT=\u00a7aPortal Frame Tint
option.PORTAL_FRAME_TINT.comment=Obsidian lit by a portal turns purple. Free, but obsidian lit by a torch or lava may get tinted too
option.ORE_LIGHT=\u00a7cOre Light
option.ORE_LIGHT.comment=Ores cast colored light onto nearby blocks, mobs and held items. The light spreads around corners like vanilla light and does not pass through walls. Heavy: an extra compute pass every frame plus a light grid lookup per pixel. Off = no cost at all
option.ORE_LIGHT_STRENGTH=\u00a7aOre Light Strength
option.ORE_LIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of the colored light from ores
option.ORE_LIGHT_RADIUS=\u00a7eOre Light Radius
option.ORE_LIGHT_RADIUS.comment=How many blocks the ore light spreads. Higher = more blocks to compute every frame = lower FPS
option.ORE_LIGHT_DIST=\u00a7eOre Light Distance
option.ORE_LIGHT_DIST.comment=Distance in blocks around you where ore light is visible. It fades in smoothly as you approach. Higher = more blocks to compute every frame = lower FPS

screen.EMISSIVE=Glowing Blocks & Mobs
screen.EMISSIVE.comment=Name color = performance cost: \u00a7agreen\u00a7r = free, \u00a7eyellow\u00a7r = small cost, \u00a7cred\u00a7r = heavy
option.ORE_GLOW=\u00a7aOre Glow
option.ORE_GLOW.comment=How brightly the colored specks of ores glow in the dark (caves, night). 0 = ores look vanilla
option.ORE_DAY_GLOW=\u00a7aOre Daylight Glow
option.ORE_DAY_GLOW.comment=Extra glow of ores in daylight so they stay visible on bright surfaces. 0 = same glow as in the dark
option.ORE_FADE_DIST=\u00a7aOre Glow Falloff Distance
option.ORE_FADE_DIST.comment=Distance in blocks at which ore glow fades to its weakest (see Ore Far Glow)
option.ORE_FAR_GLOW=\u00a7aOre Far Glow
option.ORE_FAR_GLOW.comment=Share of ore glow kept at the falloff distance and beyond. 0 = distant ores do not glow, 1 = no falloff
option.REDSTONE_GLOW=\u00a7aRedstone Glow
option.REDSTONE_GLOW.comment=Glow of redstone torches, powered redstone dust and other redstone parts. 0 = vanilla look
option.PORTAL_GLOW=\u00a7aNether Portal Glow
option.PORTAL_GLOW.comment=Brightness of the purple glowing surface of nether portals. 0 = vanilla look
option.MOB_EYES=\u00a7aMob Eye Glow
option.MOB_EYES.comment=Eyes of endermen, spiders and other mobs glow in the dark
option.MOB_EYES_GLOW=\u00a7aMob Eye Glow Strength
option.MOB_EYES_GLOW.comment=How bright mob eyes are up close
option.MOB_EYES_FADE_DIST=\u00a7aMob Eye Falloff Distance
option.MOB_EYES_FADE_DIST.comment=Distance in blocks at which eye glow fades to its weakest (see Mob Eye Far Glow)
option.MOB_EYES_FAR_GLOW=\u00a7aMob Eye Far Glow
option.MOB_EYES_FAR_GLOW.comment=Eye brightness at the falloff distance compared to the plain texture. Below 1 = dimmer than vanilla, 1 = vanilla eyes

screen.WEATHER=Weather & Snow
screen.WEATHER.comment=Name color = performance cost: \u00a7agreen\u00a7r = free, \u00a7eyellow\u00a7r = small cost, \u00a7cred\u00a7r = heavy
option.RAIN_FOG=\u00a7aRain Fog
option.RAIN_FOG.comment=Extra haze that thickens during rain when you are outdoors. Render distance stays the same. 0 = no rain haze
option.RAIN_SKY_DARKNESS=\u00a7aRain Sky Darkness
option.RAIN_SKY_DARKNESS.comment=How much darker the sky and fog get while it rains. 0 = same as in dry weather
option.RAIN_OPACITY=\u00a7aRain Opacity
option.RAIN_OPACITY.comment=How visible raindrops and snowflakes are where they are lit
option.RAIN_THINNESS=\u00a7aRain Thinness
option.RAIN_THINNESS.comment=Higher = thinner, more transparent raindrops. 0 = thick vanilla streaks
option.RAIN_BRIGHTNESS=\u00a7aRain Brightness
option.RAIN_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Brightness of raindrops and splashes. Lower = darker, grayer drops, 1 = white in daylight. Drops near fire stay lit
option.FOG_GLOW=\u00a7aTorch Glow in Fog
option.FOG_GLOW.comment=Light of torches and fires scatters in the rain haze, making a warm halo around lit places. Visible only while it rains
option.FOG_GLOW_STRENGTH=\u00a7aTorch Fog Glow Strength
option.FOG_GLOW_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of the warm halo around lights in rain haze
option.LIGHTNING_BOLT=\u00a7aBranched Lightning
option.LIGHTNING_BOLT.comment=Draws a procedural branching bolt in the sky instead of the vanilla one. Off = vanilla bolt
option.LIGHTNING_STRENGTH=\u00a7aLightning Light
option.LIGHTNING_STRENGTH.comment=How strongly a lightning flash lights up the sky and the world. 0 = no flash
option.SNOWIFY=\u00a7aSnowify World
option.SNOWIFY.comment=Winter look: grass and leaves turn frosty white, top faces under the open sky get covered with snow. Snow melts near torches and lava. Overworld only
option.SNOW_AMOUNT=\u00a7aSnow Amount
option.SNOW_AMOUNT.comment=How strongly the world is covered with snow and frost
option.SNOW_BRIGHTNESS=\u00a7aSnow Brightness
option.SNOW_BRIGHTNESS.comment=How bright snow and frost are in daylight. 1 = pure white even under the overcast sky

screen.WATER=Water & Ice
screen.WATER.comment=Name color = performance cost: \u00a7agreen\u00a7r = free, \u00a7eyellow\u00a7r = small cost, \u00a7cred\u00a7r = heavy
option.WATER_OPACITY=\u00a7aWater Opacity
option.WATER_OPACITY.comment=Opacity of the water surface seen from above. Deeper water gets murkier on its own, so the bottom fades out with depth
option.WATER_BRIGHTNESS=\u00a7aWater Brightness
option.WATER_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Brightness of the dark gray water surface
option.WATER_PATTERN=\u00a7aWater Surface Pattern
option.WATER_PATTERN.comment=How much of the water texture shows through the murk when looking from above. 0 = flat murky water
option.UNDERWATER_DENSITY=\u00a7aUnderwater Fog Density
option.UNDERWATER_DENSITY.comment=How quickly the dark blue murk swallows the view underwater and through the water surface. Higher = thicker, the bottom disappears sooner
option.ICE_OPACITY=\u00a7aIce Opacity
option.ICE_OPACITY.comment=How opaque ice and frosted ice are. Lower = more transparent

screen.FOLIAGE=Foliage
screen.FOLIAGE.comment=Name color = performance cost: \u00a7agreen\u00a7r = free, \u00a7eyellow\u00a7r = small cost, \u00a7cred\u00a7r = heavy
option.SWAY=\u00a7aFoliage Sway
option.SWAY.comment=Leaves, grass, flowers and other plants sway in the wind
option.SWAY_STRENGTH=\u00a7aSway Strength
option.SWAY_STRENGTH.comment=How far leaves and plants move
option.SWAY_SPEED=\u00a7aSway Speed
option.SWAY_SPEED.comment=How fast leaves and plants move
option.STORM_SWAY=\u00a7aStorm Sway
option.STORM_SWAY.comment=How much rain and thunderstorms boost the sway speed and amplitude. 0 = weather has no effect

screen.DIMENSIONS=Nether & End
screen.DIMENSIONS.comment=Name color = performance cost: \u00a7agreen\u00a7r = free, \u00a7eyellow\u00a7r = small cost, \u00a7cred\u00a7r = heavy
option.NETHER_BRIGHTNESS=\u00a7aNether Brightness
option.NETHER_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Brightness of the Nether ambient light and fog. Only affects dark places: lava, fire and torches stay just as bright
option.NETHER_HAZE=\u00a7eNether Heat Haze
option.NETHER_HAZE.comment=The distant view in the Nether shimmers like hot air above a fire. Nearby blocks and hands stay sharp. Small FPS cost, only in the Nether: one extra full screen pass with depth reads
option.NETHER_HAZE_STRENGTH=\u00a7aHeat Haze Strength
option.NETHER_HAZE_STRENGTH.comment=How far the shimmer bends the image
option.NETHER_HAZE_DIST=\u00a7aHeat Haze Distance
option.NETHER_HAZE_DIST.comment=Distance in blocks where the haze begins. It reaches full strength at 2.5 times this distance
option.NETHER_HAZE_SPEED_MIN=\u00a7aHeat Haze Min Speed
option.NETHER_HAZE_SPEED_MIN.comment=Slowest shimmer speed. The speed drifts smoothly between min and max like gusts of hot air. Set both equal for a constant speed
option.NETHER_HAZE_SPEED_MAX=\u00a7aHeat Haze Max Speed
option.NETHER_HAZE_SPEED_MAX.comment=Fastest shimmer speed during a gust
option.END_BRIGHTNESS=\u00a7aEnd Brightness
option.END_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Brightness of the End ambient light, sky and fog. Only affects dark places: torches stay just as bright

screen.COLOR=Color
screen.COLOR.comment=Name color = performance cost: \u00a7agreen\u00a7r = free, \u00a7eyellow\u00a7r = small cost, \u00a7cred\u00a7r = heavy
option.DESATURATION=\u00a7aDesaturation
option.DESATURATION.comment=Washes out the colors of the whole image. 0 = original colors, 1 = black and white
option.NIGHT_DESATURATION=\u00a7aDark Desaturation
option.NIGHT_DESATURATION.comment=How much colors fade to cold gray in dark areas (night, caves, shadows). 0 = dark areas keep their colors
option.HIGHLIGHT_BOOST=\u00a7aNight Highlight Boost
option.HIGHLIGHT_BOOST.comment=Makes bright spots (fire, torches, lava) brighter at night so they stand out from the darkness. No effect during the day. Always on in the Nether and the End

screen.POST=Camera Effects
screen.POST.comment=Name color = performance cost: \u00a7agreen\u00a7r = free, \u00a7eyellow\u00a7r = small cost, \u00a7cred\u00a7r = heavy
option.GLOW=\u00a7eGlow
option.GLOW.comment=Soft glow around bright areas and a light haze over the whole image. Small FPS cost
option.GLOW_STRENGTH=\u00a7aGlow Strength
option.GLOW_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of the glow around bright areas. 0 = haze only, no glow
option.CHROMA=\u00a7aChromatic Aberration
option.CHROMA.comment=Red/blue color fringing at the screen edges, like a cheap lens. The center of the screen stays clean
option.CHROMA_STRENGTH=\u00a7aAberration Strength
option.CHROMA_STRENGTH.comment=How far the red and blue channels are shifted at the edges
option.CHROMA_OPACITY=\u00a7aAberration Opacity
option.CHROMA_OPACITY.comment=How strongly the shifted colors are blended in. Lower = subtler effect
option.FILM_GRAIN=\u00a7aFilm Grain
option.FILM_GRAIN.comment=Animated film grain over the image
option.GRAIN_OPACITY=\u00a7aGrain Opacity
option.GRAIN_OPACITY.comment=How visible the grain is. Lower = more transparent
option.GRAIN_CONTRAST=\u00a7aGrain Contrast
option.GRAIN_CONTRAST.comment=Low = soft faint ripple, high = hard distinct specks
option.GRAIN_SIZE=\u00a7aGrain Size
option.GRAIN_SIZE.comment=Grain size in pixels. Above 1 = larger, softer grain
option.GRAIN_COLOR=\u00a7aGrain Color
option.GRAIN_COLOR.comment=0 = gray grain, 1 = fully colored grain
option.GRAIN_DENSITY=\u00a7aGrain Density
option.GRAIN_DENSITY.comment=Share of pixels covered by grain. Lower = sparse separate specks, 1 = dense grain everywhere
option.VIGNETTE=\u00a7aVignette
option.VIGNETTE.comment=Darkens the corners and edges of the screen

screen.AA=Anti-Aliasing & Sharpness
screen.AA.comment=Name color = performance cost: \u00a7agreen\u00a7r = free, \u00a7eyellow\u00a7r = small cost, \u00a7cred\u00a7r = heavy
option.FXAA=\u00a7eAnti-Aliasing (FXAA)
option.FXAA.comment=Smooths jagged block edges. Small FPS cost: a few extra samples per pixel, the smoothing itself runs only on contrasty edges
option.FXAA_STRENGTH=\u00a7aFXAA Strength
option.FXAA_STRENGTH.comment=How much of the smoothed image is blended in. Lower = sharper but more jagged edges
option.SHARPEN=\u00a7eSharpen
option.SHARPEN.comment=Light sharpening that brings back detail. Small FPS cost
option.SHARPEN_STRENGTH=\u00a7aSharpen Strength
option.SHARPEN_STRENGTH.comment=How strong the sharpening is. Too high = bright halos around edges

screen.HUD=Status & Interface
screen.HUD.comment=Name color = performance cost: \u00a7agreen\u00a7r = free, \u00a7eyellow\u00a7r = small cost, \u00a7cred\u00a7r = heavy
option.LOW_HEALTH=\u00a7aLow Health Effect
option.LOW_HEALTH.comment=When health is low, the screen edges pulse red with a heartbeat and colors fade
option.LOW_HEALTH_STRENGTH=\u00a7aLow Health Strength
option.LOW_HEALTH_STRENGTH.comment=How strong the low health effect is
option.LOW_AIR=\u00a7aLow Air Effect
option.LOW_AIR.comment=When you are running out of air underwater, the view darkens, narrows and loses color
option.LOW_AIR_STRENGTH=\u00a7aLow Air Strength
option.LOW_AIR_STRENGTH.comment=How strong the low air effect is
option.INTRO_TITLE=\u00a7aIntro Title
option.INTRO_TITLE.comment=Shows the shader name, version and author for a couple of seconds after loading
option.INTRO_POSITION=\u00a7aIntro Title Position
option.INTRO_POSITION.comment=Screen corner where the intro title appears
value.INTRO_POSITION.0=Top Right
value.INTRO_POSITION.1=Top Left
value.INTRO_POSITION.2=Bottom Right
value.INTRO_POSITION.3=Bottom Left
